crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_math_more_dimensions.sky:3:11: error: the argument of `expm1` must be dimensionless, found length
  |
3 | a = expm1(x)
  |           ^ this has dimension length
  = note: expm1(x) = exp(x) - 1, and exp needs a pure number
  = help: divide by a reference length, e.g. `expm1(x / (1 m))`

crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_math_more_dimensions.sky:4:11: error: the argument of `log1p` must be dimensionless, found time
  |
4 | b = log1p(2 s)
  |           ^^^ this has dimension time
  = note: log1p(x) = log(1 + x) adds x to 1, which only makes sense when x is a pure number
  = help: divide by a reference time, e.g. `log1p(x / (1 s))`

crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_math_more_dimensions.sky:5:10: error: the argument of `sinh` must be dimensionless, found velocity
  |
5 | c = sinh(5 m/s)
  |          ^^^^^ this has dimension velocity
  = note: hyperbolic functions are built from exp(x) and exp(-x), which need a pure number
  = help: divide by a reference velocity, e.g. `sinh(x / (1 m/s))`

crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_math_more_dimensions.sky:6:11: error: the argument of `atanh` must be dimensionless, found mass
  |
6 | d = atanh(1 kg)
  |           ^^^^ this has dimension mass
  = note: inverse hyperbolic functions are logarithms of expressions in a pure number x, like log(x + sqrt(x² + 1))
  = help: divide by a reference mass, e.g. `atanh(x / (1 kg))`

crates/sky-types/tests/ui/err_math_more_dimensions.sky:7:9: error: the argument of `erf` must be dimensionless, found length
  |
7 | e = erf(x)
  |         ^ this has dimension length
  = note: erf(x) integrates exp(-t²) up to x, and exp needs a pure number, so x must be one
  = help: divide by a reference length, e.g. `erf(x / (1 m))`

